&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pontera is a fintech company on a mission to help people retire better. Our software platform enables retirement savers to get the help they need managing their 401(k) and other retirement plan accounts as part of a personalized strategy by their trusted financial advisor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is used by financial advisors across the nation– from SMB to Fortune 500 RIA firms, independent broker-dealers, plan custodians, and plan advisors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading venture capital firms including ICONIQ Growth and Lightspeed Venture Partners, Pontera is built by talented individuals who share a dedication to helping people retire with greater security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is fast-growing and driven to become one of the largest fintech companies in the world.&amp;nbsp; Our culture is built on a people-first principle: in a complex and numbers-driven industry, we never lose sight of the people we serve and work alongside. That’s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;positionInfo&quot; class=&quot;careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;DESCRIPTION&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for an Event Marketing Manager to partner with our Director of Events to bring Pontera&#39;s event strategy to life. This person will play a key role in planning and executing high-impact experiences while independently owning projects and collaborating closely with Marketing and Sales. We&#39;re looking for someone who is equal parts collaborator, executor, and creative problem solver. This role is a true partnership with the Directorof Events, helping bring our event strategy to life while continuously raising the bar for how Pontera shows up in the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll support the planning and execution of our trade shows, hosted events, executive programs, and field marketing initiatives, while also owning projects independently when appropriate. You&#39;ll help transform ideas into exceptional experiences, contribute your own creative thinking, and ensure flawless execution from planning through onsite delivery.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on role for someone who thrives on both planning and execution. Whether you&#39;re developing booth concepts, coordinating vendors, managing logistics, packing materials, setting up onsite, or solving last-minute challenges, you&#39;re willing to do whatever it takes to deliver a seamless and memorable experience. At Pontera, no task is too small when it comes to creating events that leave a lasting impression.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;What Success Looks Like&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;re equally comfortable brainstorming a new booth experience as you are labeling shipping boxes, managing inventory, building a run of show, or troubleshooting onsite. You understand that exceptional events are built through thoughtful planning, meticulous execution, and a willingness to jump in wherever needed. You take pride in making the details invisible so attendees experience something extraordinary.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row noPaddingTop careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6 col-md-12 col-sm-12 positionInfo&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Director of Events to plan and execute Pontera&#39;s trade shows, conferences, hosted events, executive dinners, and field marketing programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage assigned events and projects while collaborating on larger strategic initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring creative ideas to the table and help transform event concepts into engaging, memorable brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help elevate Pontera&#39;s presence through thoughtful booth design, branded environments, and event activations that attract the right audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational execution of events, including shipping and receiving, inventory management, booth setup and teardown, registration management, vendor coordination, onsite logistics, and post-event reconciliation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate vendors, venues, agencies, shipping, travel, registration, and onsite logistics to ensure seamless execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Marketing and Sales to align event plans with business goals and campaign priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track event performance, lead tracking, maintain project plans, and identify opportunities to improve future programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manages event-level budgets, purchase orders, invoices, and expense tracking within approved plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate internal event communications, staffing plans, executive schedules, and event documentation to ensure cross-functional readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain strong relationships with vendors and industry partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage multiple projects simultaneously while maintaining exceptional organization and attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 20% to support onsite event execution, including trade shows, conferences, and hosted events. This role includes occasional lifting, shipping, booth setup, and other hands-on responsibilities to help deliver exceptional event experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;REQUIREMENTS&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset with the confidence to own projects independently while partnering closely with leadership on larger initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7 years of experience in event marketing, field marketing, or event management in a B2B Saas environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing trade shows, conferences, and industry events from planning through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in vendor management, event logistics, budgeting, and project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering cross-functionally with Marketing, Sales, and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple complex initiatives simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building event reporting and performance measurement frameworks to evaluate program success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative mindset with a passion for designing memorable brand experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working independently while collaborating effectively across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a hands-on role that requires a willingness to pitch in wherever needed to ensure every event is executed flawlessly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using Monday.com for project management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Marketo or another marketing automation platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in financial services marketing is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;: Annual Salary of $110,000-$130,000&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;: Have a major impact at a fast-growing startup that is revolutionizing the FinTech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Culture&lt;/strong&gt;: A collegial, collaborative, fun work environment with frequent team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;: All new hires are eligible for equity grant participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare&lt;/strong&gt;: Comprehensive &amp;amp; affordable insurance benefits with a variety of plan options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement&lt;/strong&gt;: 401(k) with employer match &amp;amp; employer-sponsored access to a retirement advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;: Paid parental leave &amp;amp; reimbursement program for family planning services (such as fertility treatments, adoption, or surrogacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Development&lt;/strong&gt;: Sponsored learning &amp;amp; development program (to cover classes, certifications, and more!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Food Perks&lt;/strong&gt;: Fully stocked kitchen &amp;amp; lunch reimbursement program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;: A hybrid office work model (In-Office Tues/Weds/Thurs and WFH Mon/Fri) &amp;amp; generous PTO day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pontera is a fintech company on a mission to help people retire better. Our software platform enables retirement savers to get the help they need managing their 401(k) and other retirement plan accounts as part of a personalized strategy by their trusted financial advisor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is used by financial advisors across the nation– from SMB to Fortune 500 RIA firms, independent broker-dealers, plan custodians, and plan advisors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading venture capital firms including ICONIQ Growth and Lightspeed Venture Partners, Pontera is built by talented individuals who share a dedication to helping people retire with greater security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is fast-growing and driven to become one of the largest fintech companies in the world.&amp;nbsp; Our culture is built on a people-first principle: in a complex and numbers-driven industry, we never lose sight of the people we serve and work alongside. That’s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;positionInfo&quot; class=&quot;careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;DESCRIPTION&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is seeking a highly skilled and motivated IT Specialist to join the Global IT team and lead IT operations for the New York office.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Pontera’s Global IT organization, this position works closely with Infrastructure, Security, R&amp;amp;D, and Operations teams to support secure, stable, and scalable IT operations across the company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Serving as the primary IT owner for the NY office, the role is responsible for employee support, office infrastructure, endpoint management, SaaS administration, identity operations, and operational continuity in a fast-paced fintech environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Responsibilities include hands-on operational support, infrastructure administration, endpoint and security operations, project execution, and cross-functional collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is a highly independent IT professional capable of managing operational responsibilities while collaborating within a global IT organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row noPaddingTop careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6 col-md-12 col-sm-12 positionInfo&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Onsite IT Operations &amp;amp; Employee Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the primary onsite IT owner for the NY office supporting approximately 100+ employees.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead onsite operational response and coordinate escalations during infrastructure, endpoint, or office technology incidents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical support for hardware, software, SaaS applications, conferencing systems, and office technology.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver executive and business-critical support in a fast-paced operational environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage onboarding and offboarding processes including device preparation, account provisioning, permissions management, and asset handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support office events and business activities requiring onsite IT support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely resolution of operational and technical issues impacting employee workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Infrastructure Administration &amp;amp; Office Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and support office infrastructure including enterprise networking, firewalls, wireless networks, VPN connectivity, CCTV systems, physical access control, conferencing technologies, and office AV systems, using platforms such as Fortinet, UniFi, Cato, and Zoom.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with ISPs and local vendors for troubleshooting, maintenance, and operational continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform onsite troubleshooting for network, hardware, and office infrastructure issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and administer cloud infrastructure services including &lt;strong&gt;Amazon WorkSpaces&lt;/strong&gt; environments, cloud-hosted operational platforms, and related access/connectivity workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support office expansions, relocations, cabling, and infrastructure deployment projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Datacenter &amp;amp; Technical Operations Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support operational activities related to datacenter infrastructure and internal technical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with Infrastructure and R&amp;amp;D teams on maintenance, deployments, operational readiness, and troubleshooting activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with infrastructure implementations, hardware lifecycle activities, and onsite operational support when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Endpoint Management &amp;amp; Identity Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage MacOS and Windows endpoint lifecycle operations through MDM platforms including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kandji \Iru&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Microsoft Intune&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, covering enrollment, compliance, patching, deployment, and troubleshooting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer identity and access management processes across SaaS platforms and internal systems using &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Okta&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and related identity platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provision and deprovision users, groups, permissions, and application access based on operational and security requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Security teams on endpoint compliance, remediation, and enforcement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SaaS Administration &amp;amp; Business Systems Support&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support centralized SaaS operations and lifecycle management through platforms such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Torii&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, including onboarding, licensing, troubleshooting, access governance, and operational administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and support core business and collaboration platforms including &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Google Workspace, Zoom&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;, and related SaaS environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with business stakeholders to support operational processes, business systems usage, and productivity workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with SaaS integrations, automation initiatives, and operational improvements using platforms such as &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Workato&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;BlinkOps&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Project Execution &amp;amp; Operational Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and execute onsite IT infrastructure and operational projects from planning through implementation and operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in infrastructure, security, office expansion, and automation initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support cross-functional technical projects with global IT team, Security, R&amp;amp;D and Facilities teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to process improvements and operational scalability initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation &amp;amp; Operational Ownership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear technical documentation for infrastructure, operational procedures, and support processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track operational tasks, incidents, and projects through &lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Jira\ monday.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; or equivalent platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain operational ownership, prioritization, and accountability for onsite IT operations and service delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;REQUIREMENTS&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in IT operations, infrastructure administration, or onsite corporate IT environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on experience supporting both Mac and Windows environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience managing MDM platforms including Kandji and Microsoft Intune.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience supporting office infrastructure including firewalls, switches, wireless networks, VPN connectivity, and office AV systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting SaaS administration, onboarding/offboarding workflows, and access management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with Security, R&amp;amp;D and Infrastructure teams on operational and compliance initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to independently prioritize, manage, and execute operational responsibilities with minimal supervision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and operational ownership capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting fintech or high-growth technology environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Fortinet, UniFi, Cato, Google Workspace, Okta, and Azure Entra ID.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with scripting, automation, or operational workflow orchestration platforms such as Workato or BlinkOps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting datacenter or infrastructure environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AWS environments and Amazon WorkSpaces administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications are an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT WE OFFER&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;: Annual Salary of $100,000-$130,000&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;: Have a major impact at a fast-growing startup that is revolutionizing the FinTech industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Culture&lt;/strong&gt;: A collegial, collaborative, fun work environment with frequent team events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equity&lt;/strong&gt;: All new hires are eligible for equity grant participation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Healthcare&lt;/strong&gt;: Comprehensive &amp;amp; affordable insurance benefits with a variety of plan options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Retirement&lt;/strong&gt;: 401(k) with employer match &amp;amp; employer-sponsored access to a retirement advisor&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Family Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;: Paid parental leave &amp;amp; reimbursement program for family planning services (such as fertility treatments, adoption, or surrogacy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional Development&lt;/strong&gt;: Sponsored learning &amp;amp; development program (to cover classes, certifications, and more!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Food Perks&lt;/strong&gt;: Fully stocked kitchen &amp;amp; lunch reimbursement program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work Flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;: A hybrid office work model (In-Office Tues/Weds/Thurs and WFH Mon/Fri) &amp;amp; generous PTO day
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Occasional after-hours or project-related support may be required based on operational needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is an equal opportunity employer, and all qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability status, protected veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Pontera is a fintech company on a mission to help people retire better. Our software platform enables retirement savers to get the help they need managing their 401(k) and other retirement plan accounts as part of a personalized strategy by their trusted financial advisor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pontera is used by financial advisors across the nation– from SMB to Fortune 500 RIA firms, independent broker-dealers, plan custodians, and plan advisors.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Backed by leading venture capital firms including ICONIQ Growth and Lightspeed Venture Partners, Pontera is built by talented individuals who share a dedication to helping people retire with greater security.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team is fast-growing and driven to become one of the largest fintech companies in the world.&amp;nbsp; Our culture is built on a people-first principle: in a complex and numbers-driven industry, we never lose sight of the people we serve and work alongside. That’s where you come in.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div id=&quot;positionInfo&quot; class=&quot;careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;DESCRIPTION&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mid-Market Account Executive, you will lead the sales process for some of the fastest growing and disruptive Broker-Dealers and RIAs in the space (50+ financial advisors). You will be in a high-impact role with CEO-level visibility, tasked with bringing in clients capable of changing our company’s trajectory.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job is being made available at an incredibly important time in Pontera’s trajectory, and there are many reasons it’s a great opportunity: a product with an immediate, measurable revenue impact for the client (share of wallet growth), a massive addressable market, and dominant category leadership in professional 401(k) management. There is a ton of greenspace. And we are looking for someone with grit, resiliency, and professionalism to capture this incredible opportunity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row noPaddingTop careerCard&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-6 col-md-12 col-sm-12 positionInfo&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;RESPONSIBILITIES&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead multi-threaded sales processes across C-Suite, Compliance, InfoSec, Legal, and Field Leadership. You own the deal from initial conversation through negotiation and close.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Map the buyers of our prospects. Understand the goals, plans, timeline, organizational structures, and personal motivations of your counterparts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and provide clients and prospects with detailed proposals and presentations personally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with BDRs to win meetings with key decision makers and learn about the goals of your target organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Solution Consultants (SCs) to assist in technical discovery and build an instance of Pontera that works for your client’s needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Relationship Managers (RMs) during late-stage negotiations to hand off a structured rollout plan, ensuring seamless advisor adoption post-close. All signed firms have a plan to use Pontera across their organizations (are “Growth Ready”).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Navigate risk, InfoSec, and compliance reviews of firm’s vetting Pontera (SEC, ERISA, SOC 2, custodial data privacy) and know when to deploy your internal Legal &amp;amp; Compliance SMEs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strive to continuously improve your sales process, demonstrating a willingness to test, learn, and implement best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;row&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12&quot;&gt;
&lt;h1 class=&quot;smallTitle positionSubTitle brandColoredText&quot;&gt;REQUIREMENTS&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;userDesignedContent company-description&quot;&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience in a new business and/or account management role within financial services, wealth management, or Fintech B2B SaaS&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 2 years of direct closing experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience negotiating and closing deals with a decision making committee of 3-5 people or larger&lt;/li&gt;
